{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/72763-new-benedictions","id":72763,"title":"New Benedictions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-15T12:21:04-08:00","id":72763,"title":"New Benedictions","content":"Hey there, I was just looking over the Bestowment Benedicitons for the Malleus Maleficarum, and I thought of three benedictions which I wonder if they would work in gameplay, and how the mechanics would work. Like, who would be invoked? How would they work with other Benedictions? How Long would it last? etc.<br /> <br /> The first Benediction I thought of was a Benediction where you would invoke Saint Francis, or some other such person, it it harkens back to those old tales of the saints sitting in fire, swimming in fish, or other such hazardous environments and come out without a scratch. This benediction would give the hunter a resistance to elemental or environmental damage like fire, electricity, being submerged in water or hazardous chemicals, etc. and could be used in tandem with Armour of Saint Martin...<br /> <br /> The second one I considered was one where the hunter would make a plea to Saint Dennis, the cephalophore, and gets its inspiration from the tales of saints who are killed, and yet continue on to perform whatever action they set out to do. The Benediction would of course be used to allow the hunter to continue on with a battle or action even after being killed (stabbed in the heart, decapitated, etc.) and would last for a scene. A pretty unsettling power to be sure for whoever the slain hunter is fighting, but I figure after such a feat that the Boon of Lazarus wouldn't work on the hunter after she had dropped dead. But when would this be invoked, before a battle? Before being killed? <br /> <br /> The third I actually got the idea from Hellsing, the anime\u2026Where the vampire slayer from the Vatican, Father Anderson, could produce seemingly unlimited amounts of blades to fight with, and fans speculated that he could use a miracle akin to what Jesus used to feed the crowd with the bread and fish. This benediction would basically allow the hunter to multiply whatever the hunter had to make it sufficient for the hunt. Say that they were low on ammunition and a group of monsters are breathing down their neck, with this benediction the weapon would miraculously be holding twice as many rounds as its carrying capacity. Or say a vampire is making a run for it and the hunter's car is low on gas, with this benediction the car seems to have more gas than what its even capable of holding. That's the idea at least...<br /> <br /> So what do you think? Would these add to the game? What would they be called? How would the mechanics work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T12:28:55-08:00","id":72766,"title":"","content":"Names:<br /> <br /> The Peace of St Francis<br /> The Duty of St Dennis<br /> <br /> I'm not too fond of a Benediction that invokes Jesus, but if you can think of the right saint, the Gifts of St...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T13:49:43-08:00","id":72805,"title":"","content":"I was thinking the last Benediction would invoke Saint Benedict for the miracle of divinely-granted supplies. <br /> <br /> <br /> I also think there is a better candidate for the first Benediction than St. Francis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}